       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the limit.\n\nThese are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Metformin IR 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin IR 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, and it is a common target dose.\n- **A lower starting dose,** such as 500 mg PO twice daily with meals, titrated up if the patient is new to metformin.\n\nIf 1700 mg was a typo, for example for 850 mg or 1000 mg, tell me the dose you meant. I'll enter it right away."
      }
