       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the dose is above the labeled maximum daily dose. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, and the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day. Confirming that the dose is intentional doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within labeled limits now.** Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg/day. I can enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy and the specialist.** If standard dosing has failed, the usual next step is another agent rather than more metformin. Options include a GLP-1 agonist, an SGLT2 inhibitor, or insulin. Pharmacy can review the case with the specialist.\n- **Use your institution's process for exceptions.** If the team decides an above-label dose is justified, it will usually need pharmacy or P&T sign-off. It would then be entered through that pathway and not through me.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order, or a different dose within the limit?"
      }
